# Applied to every build whose context is the repo root and that has no
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` of its own (the scheduler image). A `.dockerignore`
# next to the Dockerfile is NOT read, and a pattern without `**/` only matches at
# the context root, so everything below that must hold for nested member trees
# (ingestion/.env, packages/*/__pycache__, ...) is written recursively.

.git/
**/.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
tests/
**/tests/
*.md
!README.md

# Secrets & machine-local config. Docker ignore patterns are anchored at the build
# context root and are not recursive, so the `**/` prefix is what keeps a
# developer's ingestion/.env or fund/.env out of the image layers the member
# trees are COPY'd into. The `secrets/` files are rendered in plaintext by
# `portopt start` and reach containers only as runtime mounts.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.certs/
**/secrets/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/coverage.xml
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/

# Gitignored build and test output that accumulates in a working checkout; the
# member trees are COPY'd whole, so it would otherwise land in the image layers.
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.coverage*
**/htmlcov/
